---
import { MCP_MANUAL_PATH, NOTION, PRICING_PATH } from '@lib/compare/notion-projects-alternative';

const review = [
  'Access: the agent sees what your Notion connection can see, and nothing more',
  'Mapping: which Notion properties become which fields, statuses and types',
  'Duplicates: tasks that already exist as issues',
  'Attachments and images inside task pages',
  'People: Notion members matched to Nothing Left members',
  'History: Notion’s edit history does not come across; each issue’s history starts when it is created',
];
---

<section id="np-switch" class="border-t border-line" aria-labelledby="np-switch-title">
  <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24 grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 lg:gap-12">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <h2 id="np-switch-title" class="h2">
        Moving tasks across from Notion.
      </h2>
      <p class="prose mt-5">
        There is no native Notion importer, and nothing is moved in one click. There are two routes, and both expect you
        to check the result.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6 text-sm">
        <a class="link" href={PRICING_PATH}>
          What it costs
          <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">
            →
          </span>
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="lg:col-span-7">
      <ol class="steps-list prose text-base">
        <li>
          <strong>CSV, the dependable route.</strong> Notion exports a database as CSV, with a markdown file for each
          page.
          <a class="link font-normal" href={NOTION.export} rel="noopener">
            Notion’s export guide
            <span class="arr ext" aria-hidden="true">
              ↗
            </span>
          </a>
          Nothing Left’s generic CSV import arrives at launch.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>An agent, guided by you.</strong> Connect the same agent to Notion MCP and to Nothing Left. It reads
          your open tasks and creates the projects, tags and issues through documented tools, as you and within your
          role.
          <a class="link font-normal" href={MCP_MANUAL_PATH}>
            Connecting an agent
            <span class="arr" aria-hidden="true">
              →
            </span>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div class="panel mt-8">
        <p class="np-review-head">Review before you rely on it</p>
        <ul class="np-review">
          {review.map(item => (
            <li>{item}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .np-review-head {
    padding: 14px 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 20px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .np-review {
    padding: 6px 20px 10px;
  }
  .np-review li {
    position: relative;
    padding: 8px 0 8px 18px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 21px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .np-review li + li {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }
  .np-review li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 15px;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: 2px;
  }
</style>
